# Course & lesson authoring

**Before acting on any request to design, plan, extend, or build a course,
module, lesson, exercise bank, assessment, or interactive learning object, read
[docs/authoring/course-authoring-workflow.md](../../docs/authoring/course-authoring-workflow.md).**
It is the single entry point: classify the request into a mode (A architecture /
B planning / C implementation / D assessment), then follow that mode's ordered
gates. Do not jump straight to code.

**Name the mode and gate you are entering** so the user can redirect early.
Resume from the furthest completed gate.

Approval boundaries are owned by [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) — that section is
canonical; this rule does not restate it.
